  "id": "cultural-drift",
  "term": "cultural drift",
  "definition": "Cultural drift is the increasing difference in learned cultural traits, such as song, between populations that are separated by distance or geographic barriers. In the source, it is described as a process that can strengthen the effects of isolation and limited gene flow between populations.",
